{"step_index":44,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:28:16Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-25T04:58:16+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-25T04:58:22+05:30\nThe search for \"Gemini API Veo video generation pricing per video free tier with billing 2025 2026\" returned the following summary:\nAs of August 2026, **there is no free tier available for Veo video generation** through the Gemini API[1][2]. Access to Veo models (such as Veo 3.1) via the API is strictly through the **paid tier**[1][3].\n\n### Pricing Overview\nVeo video generation is metered on a per-second basis rather than by token usage[4]. Pricing varies depending on the model version (e.g., Standard vs. Fast) and quality settings[5][6].\n\n*   **Standard Pricing:** Rates typically start around **$0.40 to $0.75 per second** for high-fidelity video with audio, depending on the specific model variant and resolution[4][5][6].\n*   **Fast Variants:** \"Fast\" versions of the model are generally more cost-effective, with rates starting as low as **$0.15 per second**[5].\n*   **Billing:** Because it is a paid-only feature, you must have a Google Cloud project with billing enabled to use the Veo API endpoints[3][7].\n\n### Important Considerations\n*   **No Free Tier:** While other Gemini text/multimodal models offer a free tier (with usage limits), the official Google documentation and pricing pages consistently list the free tier as **\"Not available\"** for Veo video generation[1][2].\n*   **Access Channels:**\n    *   **Gemini API (Google AI Studio/Vertex AI):** This is the primary path for programmatic access and requires a paid account[8][9].\n    *   **Google AI Subscriptions:** Consumers can access Veo-powered features through Google AI Pro or Ultra subscription plans (e.g., $19.99/month for Pro), though these are generally for app-based use rather than raw API integration[5][6].\n*   **Cost Management:** Because video generation can be expensive (e.g., a single 8-second clip can cost several dollars at standard rates), it is recommended to use the \"Fast\" variants for prototyping and to implement strict budget alerts in your Google Cloud project[4][9][6].\n\n*Note: Pricing and availability can change. Always verify the live rate card in your Google Cloud Console or Google AI Studio before initiating high-volume workloads[10][9].*\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE8u1XhoQikIO272AbcPC2oyQKRjjQqvBCEgprJNNaXOg5SuFOs2Ib1UtrJyKcL10IvMMMFrm2sctT0JLqLpjBqC1bwzp6c33TiOQXuNm2GucXgbVQ7EgXlFdLGgQcqpRVBqw==)\n[2] [laozhang.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGPyWGJclqQwEDRocPwD21T27WIbERJ7xRbp6JD0FeHQy5udoID5Y-0GcZOpG2d9WQJg4e67RpWYzHP0bC-iMu3K6Bl2Y2XJ7C5KC6NgnjVhgTZwbkISy6JPcaMbRxsNwa7M1sgk1uihPYlCA==)\n[3] [veo3ai.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE5VOZSZYGhj-WwoIrYzyrvv8_kTVF6po2aguABY2AAwT5Ah7rLQuHx74TzDlILYhnrGJAEjcd1Bb1P2Vtx6W8PzJuIJgjrqSizjenn-VJxTXvoLibi25OKfUEElRJbds0JWnXESRPd1vsr3jW0Z_FmJY0L7EaglJVjbHIVG0HsuA==)\n[4] [geotoolbox.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG8nIxTLhrP8yQPEyqx5voDYv_YMWancWNCNPBntO4Oswgs9q8bumX2a369plvNHWAYGYjbjhDzscTijJH3McsVCc709Heed8fdiKL3OQ--OoQKiZgBp6mUd0YdKS21eWavhg==)\n[5] [aifreeapi.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHE4RC-mjnYKeZGj-Y9HphBUaenUM17faW6a7aMruh1jxTmxnlyJRPKPg2Dx_HJNj9qBqCumQy7jjF8PFpjcU8Glb-vx91i0TSoqs3tiHoZMD7xWAwJpqVTVHOguHL10OoOxgoPNqPZ)\n[6] [kie.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFpr2BFK9FQm3hXsVNoQoE9b6nY-545hs8R7T4ftuYXaLOIBun7wHC--ZRCtUNwZrDZoAkkNMRq7KaJzyGhHKyluSKnhqY0jr672Ya-JGCxIzXSUDld)\n[7] [googleblog.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE0EhO5gQC8_RYL6h4HP-4N8t-bBEDZMc0sdGH9cugf32ns83hOKPwNKCFTsFO57iCclU5iROsitD3AewKPplWY3e3T2Ek-Z3PLuRikqE_N9rLtXBt-FJeRn3efI0nNu5_YD2O_B_aekSgufOGwQOe