{"step_index":52,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:35:15Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-25T05:05:15+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-25T05:05:33+05:30\nThe search for \"Wan2.1 open source video generation model quality comparison 2026\" returned the following summary:\nAs of mid-2026, the **Wan 2.1** and subsequent **Wan 2.2** models from Alibaba are widely regarded as among the top-tier open-weight video generation models available[1][2][3]. They are frequently compared against other leading open-source models like **HunyuanVideo**, **LTX-Video**, and **Mochi 1**[4][1].\n\n### Quality and Performance Overview\n*   **Top-Tier Quality:** Wan models are highly praised for their cinematic quality, realistic lighting, and strong motion consistency[5][6][3]. They are often cited as setting the \"open-weights\" benchmark for visual quality[1][2].\n*   **Model Variants:** The ecosystem has evolved rapidly. While **Wan 2.1** established the foundation (using a Diffusion Transformer/DiT architecture and a specialized 3D VAE), the newer **Wan 2.2** series (released in 2025/2026) introduced **Mixture-of-Experts (MoE)** architectures to improve performance while maintaining efficient inference costs[5][7][8].\n*   **Comparison with Alternatives:**\n    *   **vs. HunyuanVideo:** Often compared for cinematic capabilities; HunyuanVideo is noted for strong prompt adherence, while Wan is frequently cited for its balanced overall quality and permissive licensing[1].\n    *   **vs. LTX-Video:** LTX-Video is favored for speed and efficiency, often performing near real-time on consumer hardware, whereas Wan models are typically chosen for higher-fidelity, cinematic outputs[4][1].\n    *   **vs. Proprietary Models:** While closed-source models like OpenAI’s Sora or Google’s Veo 3 remain powerful, Wan 2.1/2.2 has narrowed the quality gap significantly, making it a primary choice for production teams who prefer local hosting and data privacy[4][9][1].\n\n### Key Technical Strengths\n*   **Apache 2.0 Licensing:** Wan 2.2, in particular, is noted for having a permissive Apache 2.0 license, which is a major advantage for commercial use compared to some other models with usage restrictions[7][2].\n*   **Architecture:** The use of Wan-VAE (a 3D spatio-temporal variational autoencoder) allows for effective encoding/decoding of 1080p video while maintaining long-term temporal consistency[10][11].\n*   **Accessibility:** Models are designed to run on consumer-grade GPUs (like the RTX 4090), though requirements scale based on the specific version (e.g., 1.3B vs. 14B parameter models)[11][6].\n\n### Summary Table: Open-Source Landscape (2026)\n\n| Model | Best For | Standout Feature |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Wan 2.2** | Best Overall Quality | High-fidelity, cinematic, permissive (Apache 2.0)[1][2] |\n| **LTX-Video** | Speed/Efficiency | Near real-time generation on consumer hardware[4][1] |\n| **HunyuanVideo** | Prompt Adherence | Strong cinematic output and instruction following[1] |\n| **Mochi 1** | Fluid Motion | High-fidelity motion, Apache licensed[1] |\n\n***Note:** The AI video landscape changes rapidly. When selecting a model, verify the latest model weights on platforms like Hugging Face or ModelScope, as newer versions (e.g., Wan 2.5+) may have been released since your last check[7][3].*\n\nSources:\n[1] [morphic.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFyOuvFjtYpOxJjq2K92GAHuZA27Ao4uAPI1e3bhMUjNS7MHGgxF9ucntLKyh5i0H1Pz2TTcPkO_l8nPokx5xk5zs3WZ5jy0jhA17wXM8m9Xu2WWhTYkp4RvZhDBcD37GptTVsSjvmq_-Z85qqn4CDOwNiYjVDwOb83PA==)\n[2] [tryinfer.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQECHtcYbL_z6fqL3LyVIhNZd7XKCAcTTHUd9uOeXqjpchY1V91CdxXJWGBQGwXz-eQC0PZreJKNin1J5MP_IhnJDHXDB8XQjFMineLEWI3bJeeb2dCWhKdlc2gtvcWp4Zmifc0wNQ==)\n[3] [vijaytalksai.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFNettmfxl1TMDHY-8Smoh_zBQLaqMJMS_t88vH