{"step_index":54,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:35:40Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-25T05:05:40+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-25T05:05:46+05:30\nThe search for \"run open source video generation model free cloud GPU no cost Colab Kaggle 2026\" returned the following summary:\nIn 2026, running open-source video generation models for free is possible through cloud notebook platforms, though you will face limitations on compute time, hardware, and session duration[1][2][3].\n\n### **Top Free Cloud GPU Platforms**\nThese platforms provide free Jupyter-style notebook environments that can run open-source models like **Wan 2.2**, **LTX-Video**, **HunyuanVideo**, or **CogVideoX**[4][5][6].\n\n*   **Google Colab**:\n    *   **What you get**: Access to a shared NVIDIA T4 GPU (16GB VRAM)[7][3].\n    *   **Limits**: No guaranteed uptime; sessions are capped at 12 hours, and you may face idle timeouts after ~90 minutes[1][8]. Resources are dynamic and subject to availability[1][9].\n    *   **Best for**: Prototyping, testing, and learning[4][10].\n*   **Kaggle Notebooks**:\n    *   **What you get**: A predictable quota of ~30 hours of free GPU (often P100 or 2× T4) per week[2][11][12].\n    *   **Limits**: Weekly reset; sessions capped at 9–12 hours[13][2].\n    *   **Note**: Kaggle is intended for data science and competitions; excessive GPU use for non-competition tasks can lead to account restrictions[11][12].\n*   **Hugging Face ZeroGPU**:\n    *   **What you get**: Access to high-end GPUs (like H200) specifically for hosting Spaces[2].\n    *   **Limits**: Limited quota on the free tier, but it is one of the most powerful options available at no cost[2].\n\n### **How to Run Video Models**\nBecause video models are resource-heavy, you should look for specific implementations optimized for lower VRAM[14][6]:\n1.  **Select a Model**: \n    *   **Wan 2.2** (Apache 2.0) is highly recommended for commercial safety and can run with memory offloading on modest hardware[15][6].\n    *   **LTX-Video** is known for speed and native audio generation[15][14].\n    *   **HunyuanVideo 1.5** is often cited for high-quality motion and can run on ~14GB VRAM with FP8/CPU offloading[15][14].\n2.  **Implementation**: Search for \"ComfyUI\" or \"GGUF\" versions of these models on Hugging Face. ComfyUI is the industry-standard interface for running these models efficiently in notebook environments[14][16].\n\n### **Important Limitations to Keep in Mind**\n*   **\"Free\" vs. \"Owned\"**: You are borrowing cloud hardware, not owning it[3]. You cannot run persistent, long-term servers on the free tiers of these platforms[8][17].\n*   **Memory Constraints**: Even with 16GB of VRAM (typical for free T4 GPUs), some high-end video models may struggle without \"offloading\" techniques (moving parts of the model to system RAM), which significantly slows down generation[15][8].\n*   **Alternatives**: If you have a decent local GPU (16GB+ VRAM), running models locally using tools like **Pinokio** or **ComfyUI** is the most reliable way to avoid cloud costs, idle timeouts, and session limits entirely[18][6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [joshthompson.co.uk](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFHzcgPbivMn5i-mO4chlYBYyiYHqLIA9rdulMXiTVSt2bQm5AGe_YFpQrL5RUcLwSaTxCE_cXGbH4S_VZi1IgGD4hzrEdIX0FFGWDEZCtUfTk4-v8PPeEIxoXlN4QUqiVFlohJ1P-Wt7ex24bT1cYfM55js6p1tCw-Yto1YE87Eq5f9ICv10Ut3086Asf2)\n[2] [gmicloud.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF3Un9ynob3HYq5j4ER3jxRepOK8tfzgCDepvxubBPvgzcU5f5dZ-HbW0hrgGrILzi-Fc0-0hvaV7RdFnKhw_YRj4t1Os4rbFM34Sti69avBFv5DaJGaaqrNI-kz7b8J0aLl-_Kh2JPGiPXPU_JqRuEi_F5QK2bx1ntIOJ025eN_lBQpJ7HdWOXNHvFZFcFCuKz)\n[3] [alibaba.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGYBJqdZQ8KeXL88r20JfqnhwMDuq45YmUby1Ur3x5NS7sli7Bcp3dP14EWgx3J9ZPuQ78MU2j4wF48Ne2x-lD4-xDwhoEmsiKJ0OgCb-l5RnlBSkrIdsQaJKnC1e4E_-L7DU2gvEU7Y2x-9vllhr18ws66ZK