{"step_index":60,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:43:32Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-25T05:13:32+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-25T05:13:38+05:30\nThe search for \"Google Cloud GPU VM pricing T4 L4 per hour Compute Engine 2026 India\" returned the following summary:\nAs of August 2026, Google Cloud GPU pricing for NVIDIA T4 and L4 instances in India (typically the `asia-south1` Mumbai region) is structured primarily through on-demand, Spot, and committed use models[1][2][3].\n\n### **NVIDIA L4 Pricing (G2 Machine Series)**\nThe L4 GPU is typically offered as part of the G2 accelerator-optimized machine family[2][4]. Pricing varies based on the machine configuration (vCPU/RAM)[3].\n\n*   **On-Demand (Estimated):** In the Mumbai region, hourly rates for L4-based instances (e.g., `g2-standard-4`) generally range from approximately **₹60 to ₹100+ per hour** for the instance, depending on the specific vCPU and memory configuration selected[1][3]. \n    *   *Note:* Global benchmarks suggest base L4 pricing often starts around **$0.318–$0.560/hr** per GPU for the accelerator portion alone, but total instance costs in India will include the underlying VM resources (vCPU/RAM)[5][3].\n*   **Spot Pricing:** Using Spot VMs can offer significant discounts (up to 60–90% depending on availability) compared to on-demand rates[6][3].\n\n### **NVIDIA T4 Pricing (N1 Machine Series)**\nThe NVIDIA T4 is a more mature, cost-effective GPU often attached to N1 general-purpose instances[7][2].\n*   While specific real-time rates for India are dynamic, T4 instances generally carry a lower hourly footprint than L4s[8]. \n*   Because T4s are often attached to N1 instances, you are billed for the GPU add-on fee plus the base cost of the N1 VM[8].\n\n### **Important Pricing Factors in India**\n*   **Currency & Billing:** Google Cloud lists prices in USD; however, if you are billed in INR, the platform applies the prevailing exchange rate to the usage[9][10]. \n*   **Region Availability:** In India, these GPUs are primarily available in **`asia-south1` (Mumbai)** and occasionally **`asia-south2` (Delhi)**[11][2]. Always check the [Google Cloud Pricing Calculator](https://cloud.google.com/products/calculator) for the most accurate quote for your specific configuration.\n*   **Discounts:**\n    *   **Committed Use Discounts (CUDs):** For predictable, long-term workloads, CUDs can provide 37–57% savings over on-demand pricing[6].\n    *   **Spot VMs:** Ideal for fault-tolerant, batch processing, or CI/CD workloads where you can withstand interruptions[6].\n*   **Additional Costs:** Remember that total costs include more than just the GPU hourly rate; you must account for **persistent disk storage, network egress (data transfer out), and potentially specialized image licenses**[9][12][13].\n\n**Recommendation:** To get the exact hourly rate for your specific project, use the **[Google Cloud Pricing Calculator](https://cloud.google.com/products/calculator)** and select your desired Mumbai region, GPU model (T4 or L4), and VM machine type to see the real-time estimate in INR[11][3].\n\nSources:\n[1] [acecloud.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEUPIP1UtlSObzfzcjlxWCcKpw8dTTKH-tlvQEBFaYIz-n6r7Qqag6BXH0m2QypPL_ea3xvLQlQbItVeCVbVyVXfxbkdu1Ko3wXV1Hrh0ZkRuEw2ghe8OiMy-bLjLxI2bdSq9j_SInlcwNcRBU=)\n[2] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQExOnwqwC2tTfYo-xIuqNB5mRUaprHmjUjoH-Sl2HQPCDXm7199n1ky5ui9lUyo_r-D3Q_XnW4Nyqn2Xz-DSONpoEizh-3T59Vs65qpToKMbyqiBaFc_SiN4sdOGeM3G6X72Y0Rji99Qx2yfhWc0vQmW3EjQFXeSSK22LQRNKs5xA==)\n[3] [gcloud-compute.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF8D13bkhbp8MBNFV824YWs3Oq9UASCqUCpvlBnPteSLXXfGQDRdQ9iDM3CRNzlEBl6nwnW-xwrxHGY0HulgmB0NsvXXDz6r_SZutW-LpWBa5ZqBk1rw_rbZA==)\n[4] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEB1I0UPSmDK3t9g375dTdr8UCSpr4qcS_